tags: []
dek: >-
  Eleven AI search agencies compared by what they can prove, with the real
  cost of each one, the eight agencies we cut for publishing nothing, and how
  to tell a GEO specialist from an SEO agency that renamed a page.
quickAnswer: >-
  Omniscient Digital is the strongest pick for mid-market B2B software.
  Breadchaser.ai is the only agency here that publishes a price for AI search
  work, $997 a month, and it is one year old. NoGood suits consumer brands
  that need each engine tracked separately. Expect $3,000 to $10,000 a month,
  and above $20,000 at the top end. Four of the eleven publish no price at
  all.
keyTakeaways:
  - >-
    Best for mid-market B2B software: Omniscient Digital. Moved one client's
    AI citation share from 15% to 35% in 60 days.
  - >-
    Best per-engine reporting: NoGood. Separate scores for Perplexity,
    ChatGPT and Gemini across 10 months.
  - >-
    Only real GEO price: Breadchaser.ai, $997/mo. Founded 2025, one case
    study.
  - >-
    Only about 17% of sources cited in Google AI Overviews also rank in the
    organic top 10 ([BrightEdge, February
    2026](https://www.brightedge.com/resources/weekly-ai-search-insights/ai-overviews-one-year-presence-size-citing)).
  - >-
    Ask which tier includes GEO. RevenueZen's $3,000 entry tier includes
    none of it.
  - >-
    Two agencies other lists call independent were acquired in early 2024.
  - >-
    A tracking dashboard costs $95 a month. Start there if you cannot name
    the prompts you want to win.
lastUpdated: 2026-08-10
metaTitle: Best GEO Agencies and AI SEO Agencies in 2026 | Verified
metaDescription: >-
  We checked 24 GEO agencies against their own sites. Eleven publish AI
  search results with timeframes. Two were acquired and still listed as
  independent.
intro: >-
  AI answers name three or four companies and stop. No page two, no
  scrolling, no second place worth having.


  Ranking well does not get you in. Only about 17% of the sources cited in
  Google AI Overviews also rank in the organic top 10, and that share has
  been flat for months ([BrightEdge, February
  2026](https://www.brightedge.com/resources/weekly-ai-search-insights/ai-overviews-one-year-presence-size-citing)).


  So every SEO agency now sells generative engine optimization, and almost
  none of them can show you a result. Eleven agencies worth a call, sorted by
  what each one can prove. We checked 24 against their own websites and cut
  13.
items:
  - rank: 1
    name: Omniscient Digital
    url: https://beomniscient.com
    startingPrice: >-
      Custom. $10,000/mo covers full-service engagements across content,
      SEO and AI search
    bestFor: >-
      Mid-market B2B software companies that already publish and want AI
      citations measured
    description: >-
      Omniscient Digital is a content and SEO agency for B2B software
      companies. Generative engine optimization sits on its own service page
      rather than as a line inside a content retainer.


      Omniscient Digital reports AI visibility as two numbers instead of
      one: how often a brand appears across tracked queries, and what share
      of citations that brand wins. A brand can appear more often and still
      be cited less, and a single blended score hides that.


      The Convert case study covers a 60-day engagement. Visibility across
      tracked queries went from 31% to 55%, which Omniscient Digital labels
      an 81% increase. It is 77%. Citation share went from 15% to 35%,
      labelled a 140% increase. It is 133%. Rounding of the underlying
      decimals is the likely explanation, and the direction of both results
      holds. Convert's CMO separately reported roughly 200% growth in AI
      Overview citations measured in Ahrefs.
